{
  "_notes": [
    "AC/DC (acd_163, Stern SAM).",
    "Derived from the matching AC/DC decoder layout and verified against local NVRAM data.",
    "SAM stores the 4 player scores as 4 x 8-byte (64-bit little-endian) fields: stride 8, not 4. The prior stride-4/length-4 layout mis-read players 2-4 (P2 read the zero high-bytes of P1, etc.). Corrected and validated against real 2-/3-/4-player Metallica dumps (mtl_180h)."
  ],
  "_fileformat": 0.8,
  "_metadata": {
    "version": 4,
    "copyright": [
      "Copyright (C) 2026 by Tom Collins <tom@scorbit.io>",
      "Copyright (C) 2026 by Andre Santana <herrmirto@proton.me>"
    ],
    "license": "GNU Lesser General Public License v3.0",
    "platform": "stern-sam",
    "roms": [
      "acd_163"
    ]
  },
  "game_state": {
    "player_count": {
      "_notes": [
        "Stern SAM number-of-players-in-game at fixed NVRAM address 0x02110900 (adjacent to game_over 0x02110904 in the SAM game-state header). Identified from three real played dumps: the only byte that reads exactly 2 / 3 / 4 in 2-, 3- and 4-player games (mtl_180h)."
      ],
      "label": "Player Count",
      "start": "0x02110900",
      "encoding": "int",
      "length": 1
    },
    "scores": [
      {
        "label": "Player 1",
        "start": "0x02110A0C",
        "encoding": "int",
        "length": 8
      },
      {
        "label": "Player 2",
        "start": "0x02110A14",
        "encoding": "int",
        "length": 8
      },
      {
        "label": "Player 3",
        "start": "0x02110A1C",
        "encoding": "int",
        "length": 8
      },
      {
        "label": "Player 4",
        "start": "0x02110A24",
        "encoding": "int",
        "length": 8
      }
    ],
    "game_over": {
      "_notes": [
        "Live-validated on representative AC/DC revisions 1.21, 1.63H, 1.65H, and non-H 1.70: 0x02110904 bit 0x40 is set in attract/game-over and clear during live and inter-ball states; this sibling's attract NVRAM also has the bit set."
      ],
      "label": "Game Over",
      "start": "0x02110904",
      "encoding": "bool",
      "mask": "0x40"
    },
    "credits": {
      "_notes": [
        "Stern SAM platform-wide credits counter at fixed NVRAM address 0x0211100C (redundant copy at 0x02111014). Identified by the stimulus-response harness (identify_game_state.py): the byte rises as coins are inserted and drops by exactly 1 when a game starts - a pricing-agnostic signature. Confirmed on mtl_180h, trn_174, avs_170, xmn_150."
      ],
      "label": "Credits",
      "start": "0x0211100C",
      "encoding": "int",
      "length": 1
    }
  },
